# Required patala-py cargo features for Cackle's `-tags patala` build.
#
# internal/payments/patala.go calls patala.PatalaFiatProviders() and
# patala.PatalaRailNewFiat(...) — both are UniFFI exports that only exist in
# the generated Go bindings when patala-py's cdylib was built with the fiat
# adapters compiled in. A cdylib built with the default (empty) feature set
# only exports the Mock rail constructors, and `go build -tags patala` then
# fails with "undefined: patala.PatalaFiatProviders" — a correct compile
# error, but a confusing one if you don't already know this file exists.
#
# This is the single source of truth for that feature set. Makefile's
# `patala-generate` target and scripts/check-patala-bindings.sh both read it,
# so there is exactly one place to update if the required surface changes —
# not three copies (a Makefile recipe, a doc comment, a script) that can
# silently drift from each other the way the underlying bug here happened:
# an earlier regeneration ran patala-go's bare `make generate` (features
# default to empty) instead of `make FEATURES=fiat-all generate`, and nothing
# caught the mismatch until `go build -tags patala` failed downstream.
#
# Do not hand-edit the generated bindings to work around a mismatch here —
# regenerate them: `make patala-generate` (or `build-patala`/`test-patala`,
# which depend on it) reads this file and does it correctly for you.
fiat-all
